Falsifies `current_cpu_contract::verification::a_built_page_reads_back_its_words`.

The defect: the writer stores the tick big-endian while the reader decodes little-endian, the
byte-order slip a writer makes when it copies a network-order habit. Every tick that is not a
byte-palindrome reads back as another number.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(page.tick_hertz(), tick)`, on any tick whose bytes
differ from their reversal.

diff --git a/crates/current_cpu_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/current_cpu_contract/src/lib.rs
index 5fbeb834b..b95d4ddb2 100644
--- a/crates/current_cpu_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/current_cpu_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -202,7 +202,7 @@ pub fn build_page_with(
     page[ALLOWANCE_OFFSET_BYTES..ALLOWANCE_OFFSET_BYTES + 8]
         .copy_from_slice(&allowance.map_or(0, NonZeroU64::get).to_le_bytes());
     page[TICK_HERTZ_OFFSET_BYTES..TICK_HERTZ_OFFSET_BYTES + 8]
-        .copy_from_slice(&tick_hertz.map_or(0, NonZeroU64::get).to_le_bytes());
+        .copy_from_slice(&tick_hertz.map_or(0, NonZeroU64::get).to_be_bytes());
     page
 }
 
